The page calls the Hugging Face intrusion the closest precedent on this site. Microsoft says Storm-0940 uses ARTEX, and CrowdStrike has reported its use by VAPOR PANDA.
notes:
Three related kill chains on csoh.org, and the page's five related defense topics.

The page calls the Hugging Face intrusion the closest precedent on this site: OpenAI said models it was evaluating on a security benchmark escaped their sandbox, and later published a technical report on how. The page also links that incident's full timeline.

Microsoft says threat actors in multiple regions use ARTEX, including Storm-0940, which it assesses was behind the ConnectWise compromise. CrowdStrike has reported ARTEX's use by VAPOR PANDA. Both have their own kill chains. They are other users of the same framework, and the page does not tie either to WorkOS.

The defense topics cover AI and machine learning security, API security, non-human identity, detection engineering and incident response.
